---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/utils';
---

<PageLayout title="About — Clean Snacks" description="The thinking behind Clean Snacks — why every recipe uses 5 real ingredients or fewer.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-dark-text mb-6">Why this exists</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-bark dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        Walk down any snack aisle and count the ingredients you recognize. You won't need both hands. Even the "healthy" options — the protein bars, the veggie chips, the organic fruit snacks — are ultra-processed products with ingredient lists that read like chemistry homework.
      </p>

      <p>
        We built Clean Snacks around one idea: <strong>what if you just made it yourself?</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Not a meal prep marathon. Not a weekend baking project. Just simple snacks made with real ingredients, ready in minutes. The kind of food that existed before the snack industry did.
      </p>

      <h2>What we stand for</h2>

      <h3>Every Ingredient Earns Its Place</h3>
      <p>
        Every recipe on this site uses ingredients you can identify on sight and find at any grocery store. No protein isolates. No maltodextrin. No "natural flavors." If it needs a lab, it doesn't belong here.
      </p>

      <h3>Five Ingredients or Fewer</h3>
      <p>
        The simpler a recipe, the more likely you are to make it again. Most of our recipes use three to five whole foods. Some use two. Complexity is the enemy of consistency.
      </p>

      <h3>No Refined Sugar</h3>
      <p>
        We sweeten with Medjool dates, raw honey, pure maple syrup, and ripe bananas — ingredients that bring minerals and fiber alongside the sweetness. Your taste buds adjust faster than you'd expect.
      </p>

      <h3>Fuel, Not Filler</h3>
      <p>
        Snacks should do something for you. We build recipes around ingredients that are naturally rich in minerals — nuts, seeds, cacao, coconut, sea salt, dark leafy greens. These are building blocks, not empty calories.
      </p>

      <h3>For Every Age and Every Moment</h3>
      <p>
        Packing a lunchbox. Fueling a workout. Reaching for something during a movie. There's a clean version of whatever you're craving. We organize by occasion because that's how snacking actually works.
      </p>

      <h2>What we're not</h2>
      <p>
        We're not a diet. We're not selling supplements. We don't count calories. We believe that when you eat real food in its whole form, your body handles the rest. The point isn't restriction — it's knowing exactly what you're eating because you made it yourself.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href={url('/recipes/')}>Browse our recipes</a> and see how simple it gets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
